{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition","id":1265029,"title":"Werewolf 5th Edition????","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-06T11:29:55-08:00","id":1265029,"title":"Werewolf 5th Edition????","content":"I just wanted to say that I was reading the Vampire 5th Edition and I think it is absolutely gorgeous! I really have to admire the team that put it together, both from an artistic point of view as well as a system streamlining point of view. But I need to ask the question, are the other game lines going to get a similar reboot or has that not been decided yet. Vampire 5th edition indicates the existence of Werewolves, Mages and Fairies so I can only hope so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T11:41:45-08:00","id":1265036,"title":"","content":"Jason Carl,from White Wolf,said they're doing werewolf. Dhaunae de Vir told me they haven't forgotten demon the fallen either","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T11:58:53-08:00","id":1265045,"title":"","content":"How about Mage...and Wraith...and Changeling?????...and Mummy????","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T12:01:23-08:00","id":1265047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265045#post1265045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Mage...and Wraith...and Changeling?????...and Mummy????</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no direct confirmation. But it would be weird if they didn't do them. My take? They be trusting onyx path to do mage and changeling and wraith for a few years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T12:43:36-08:00","id":1265074,"title":"","content":"For all intents and purposes, yes there is indeed a Werewolf 5e being planned. W20 ended with Changing Ways because of that.<br /> <br /> How soon it's coming, we don't know. NuWW referenced it a few times in past conferences and panels, but since this year it hasn't been talked about further. Not even as V5's corebook officially launched. We don't even have any confirmed release window on when it would come out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265045#post1265045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about Mage...and Wraith...and Changeling?????...and Mummy????</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where the direct source is, but nuWW has stated that they want to make new WoD5 editions for ALL of the gamelines. How soon they're coming though, nobody knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T12:49:52-08:00","id":1265076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265074#post1265074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all intents and purposes, yes there is indeed a Werewolf 5e being planned. W20 ended with Changing Ways because of that.<br /> <br /> How soon it's coming, we don't know. NuWW referenced it a few times in past conferences and panels, but since this year it hasn't been talked about further. Not even as V5's corebook officially launched. We don't even have any confirmed release window on when it would come out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure where the direct source is, but nuWW has stated that they want to make new WoD5 editions for ALL of the gamelines. How soon they're coming though, nobody knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>OMG!!! This is making me excited beyond belief. I cannot wait to see the exciting new directions these game lines are going into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T15:15:38-08:00","id":1265130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265074#post1265074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all intents and purposes, yes there is indeed a Werewolf 5e being planned. W20 ended with Changing Ways because of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 has officially ended? Well, <i>damn</i>. Still, that explains why I haven't seen any new titles past Changing Ways for W20. I was wondering a bit about that.<br /> <br /> As for the idea of a Werewolf 5th, I was a bit leery of the idea of Vampire 5th, but I have to reserve judgment until I actually <i>read</i> V5th. Same for W5th.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T15:20:00-08:00","id":1265131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265074#post1265074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all intents and purposes, yes there is indeed a Werewolf 5e being planned. W20 ended with Changing Ways because of that.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Only other thing planned was Bunyip tb....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T21:24:43-08:00","id":1265212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265130#post1265130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 has officially ended? Well, <i>damn</i>. Still, that explains why I haven't seen any new titles past Changing Ways for W20. I was wondering a bit about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. <br /> <br /> I believe the only thing left of W20 to be made is &quot;The Art of W20&quot;. Otherwise that's it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265131#post1265131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only other thing planned was Bunyip tb....</div> </div> </div> </div>...which in the comments of an MMN, Rich confirmed TB Bunyip has been shelved due to nuWW wanting to move forward with W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T21:30:30-08:00","id":1265213,"title":"","content":"I think Werewolf: The Apocalypse 5th Edition is probably going to be available about this time next year, and I'll be interested in the outcome. Personally, I think having 'Rage Dice' as per V5's 'Hunger Dice' would add a really effective dimension to the game, and while I think Werewolf ought to keep it's core themes in tact, I feel they could a dd a lot more edge in it's presentation. I'd like to see Werewolves look <i>scary</i> again and the art direction would play a big role in that.<br /> <br /> The other thing I'd like to see, which has always been present but could use more emphasis is the formation of the Pack. I'd like to see a bit less macro-politics based on the thirteen Tribes (which would still be there, nevertheless) but create a more survival-in-isolation feel for the PCs - more defending the territory than big tribal societies. While the various changing breeds could still be there, I'd like to see less of them in the core game (and not as playable characters till the supplements).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-07-2018, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T21:39:21-08:00","id":1265214,"title":"","content":"Tribebook Bunyip got shelved? Man, I was really looking forward to that. We got enough tribal information in Croatan Song for the Croatan, we got the White Holwers tribebook after waiting for years for it, but we're losing Tribebook Bunyip? That's disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T09:36:51-08:00","id":1265298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265074#post1265074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all intents and purposes, yes there is indeed a Werewolf 5e being planned. W20 ended with Changing Ways because of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That book was so bad it ended an entire game line <b>*badum-tss!*</b><br /> I'm quite hopeful for the new W5, i have to say. It's coming a bit too early for my taste but if there's a thing that Werewolf needs is a streamlining of combat mechanics- and V5 did just that. I expect them to apply the same system to the game and who knows, perhaps I'll be able with that to end my battles in less than an hour.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit worried about how they're going to handle the setting, though. After all the polemics on the Nazi feeling of V5 I fear they'll try to pander to their hypersensitive fans and publish a watered down edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-07-2018, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T10:46:14-08:00","id":1265315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265074#post1265074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all intents and purposes, yes there is indeed a Werewolf 5e being planned. W20 ended with Changing Ways because of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sad, as I was hoping for a Werewolf equivalent of Beckett's Jyhad Diary to wrap it up and set up W5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T11:40:08-08:00","id":1265331,"title":"","content":"I am really excited about a werewolf reboot, here are some thoughts.<br /> <br /> 1/ Keep it scary. Werewolf seemed to become a cartoon after a while which was not really fitting for a game of savage horror<br /> <br /> 2/ Less whining. I was always puzzled about how werewolves were lamenting that they were fighting a losing battle and yet a pack of werewolves could cause enough damage to sink a battleship. Make some enemies that really can kill a pack of werewolves rather than just being claw fodder.<br /> <br /> 3/ Make going into a rage a real danger. Werewolf the forsaken had a good idea with Basu-Ilm but it didn't seem to go far enough with the dangers of doing it (it seemed more of a big red button which says WIN BATTLE). The Second Inquisition gives more reason that Werewolves need to stay hidden lest the CIA start hunting them down.<br /> <br /> 4/ More problems that involve more solutions than just turning to Crinos and beating the hell out of the offending obstacle. <br /> <br /> 5/ More, and deadlier, pack vs. pack and tribe vs. tribe conflict. Does everyone really have to be on the same team???<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T14:14:01-08:00","id":1265380,"title":"","content":"1/ So having an utterly remorseless enemy consisting of an entire third of the fabric of reality itself is not scary enough for you? An enemy of which only a small part of its army consists of utterly insane werewolves who represent everything you could become if you lose yourself too much to your Rage? An enemy capable of turning you into one of them if they capture you and make you dance the Black Spiral if they don't torture you to death first? An enemy that is winning the war to <i>decide the fate of the universe</i> despite all your best efforts? All this by you isn't scary?<br /> <br /> 2/ &quot;Less whining?&quot; You're talking about &quot;less whining&quot; when the Garou's morale in fighting a war to save the world is at (and in the case of Garou suffering under Harano, even past) the breaking point? Losing a war is <i>supposed</i> to be depressing precisely because of all the things that are at stake. As for &quot;making some enemies that can actually kill a pack of werewolves,&quot; did you forget about the aforementioned Black Spiral Dancers? Did you forget about the BSDs and Pentex's First Teams that have actually attacked and destroyed Garou septs, taken Garou caerns and converted them to Wyrmholes and Pits? Did you forget the minions of the Weaver who are almost as dangerous as the Wyrm? Did you forget that the last member of the Triat, the Wyld, can't even be counted as an ally precisely because its chaotic nature is so dangerous? Banes, formori, BSDs, and FRICKIN' NEXUS CRAWLERS aren't sufficiently dangerous to kill a werewolf pack? Seriously?<br /> <br /> 3/ &quot;Make going into rage a real danger.&quot; Succumbing to Rage isn't dangerous enough with the threat of falling into the Thrall of the Wyrm? Of losing control so thoroughly that you fall to cannibalism, rape or being unable to tell the difference between allies and enemies as you lose your literal self to a red haze of madness? This by you isn't dangerous?<br /> <br /> 4/ If you want problems that can't be solved just by ripping it to shreds, what about the afore-mentioned Pentex and all the industries it's corrupted and all the politicians it's bought or sidelined? You can't kill them without endangering the Veil. And even if you did manage to keep the Veil intact after killing the captains of industry or holders of political office, what then? The people you killed will just get replaced. There's a reason that Pentex is known as the Hydra. Did you forget the short story in W20 Book of the Wyrm where the Glass Walker kills everyone in a Pentex board room and the last Pentex guy standing blows cigar smoke into the Garou's face and says &quot;All this aftermath from a terrorist attack is just going to make our stock <i>rise</i>&quot;? The idea of how to fight a polluting corporation without resorting to ecoterrorism and creating a backlash that defeats the Garou anyway has been one of W:tA's main themes since Pentex was first introduced waaaaay back in the original Book of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> /5 Not enough tribe vs tribe conflict? Let's take a close look at that, shall we? The Black Furies and the Get of Fenris hate each other. The Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs are at odds over leading the Garou Nation. The Wendigo and Uktena are still upset with the European tribes (especially the Fianna, Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs) for taking their caerns and slaughtering their Kin during America's Manifest Destiny period. The Bone Gnawers are looked down upon by <i>almost all</i> the other Tribes (except the Glass Walkers and CoG) for being mongrels. The Red Talons hate all the other tribes for even having human kinfolk and REALLY hate the Glass Walkers for being influenced by the Weaver and living in cities. The theme that the Garou have always been at odds with each other and can't team up effectively to save Gaia has been there ever since 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> maryshelly, everything you're looking for in Werewolf has been there from the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 11-07-2018, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T01:19:31-08:00","id":1265463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265214#post1265214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tribebook Bunyip got shelved? Man, I was really looking forward to that. We got enough tribal information in Croatan Song for the Croatan, we got the White Holwers tribebook after waiting for years for it, but we're losing Tribebook Bunyip? That's disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> NuWW de-canoned Shattered Dreams.....screwed with Changing Ways.....got TB Bunyip cancelled......I mean after reading and playing V5 they were pushing shit uphill to make me give them a chance but they're doing they're best to actively piss WtA fans off. But I guess if they're looking at basing it on the stuff they signed off on for BNS WtA we're all gonna be pissed off anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T03:29:03-08:00","id":1265470,"title":"","content":"What's BNS?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T03:36:19-08:00","id":1265471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265298#post1265298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a bit worried about how they're going to handle the setting, though. After all the polemics on the Nazi feeling of V5 I fear they'll try to pander to their hypersensitive fans and publish a watered down edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Werewolf's drifting to that direction. If Vampire is subtle, Werewolf is raw. Hate, rascism, war, violence, primitivity, sexism - all of this marked Werewolf. Taking them from WtA would be dissapointing, it will be absolutly new game, it won't be WtA. On facebook WW showed a new WtA logo, with glyph of war and modern anarchic mood. I hope it's announcement of something in old brutal style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T04:24:45-08:00","id":1265478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265470#post1265470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's BNS?</div> </div> </div> </div>By Night Studios. The Onyx Path of LARPs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T16:47:15-08:00","id":1265616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265213#post1265213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Werewolf: The Apocalypse 5th Edition is probably going to be available about this time next year,.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine we'd have seen an alpha slice by now.<br /> <br /> I expect its going to be Chicago, Something else, Sabbat next year. and Werewolf in 2020. Mage is probably even further out as it still has books same with c20 and wr20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T18:19:31-08:00","id":1265633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265463#post1265463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I guess if they're looking at basing it on the stuff they signed off on for BNS WtA we're all gonna be pissed off anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's what they're doing. Not entirely, at least.<br /> <br /> BNS WtA had the whole thing about the Garou Nation splitting up into different factions. However, BNS has admitted that it's less to do with nuWW executive direction and more to do with adapting to a LARP. That because the type of gameplay of a LARP is completely different from a TRPG, that changes had to be made. In this case, that LARP is more suited to politicking gameplay, and WtA TRPG setting wasn't as suited to it the same way that Vampire and Changeling are. Apparently, moot politicking wasn't a good enough hook, and (from my time looking at WtA communities), that tends to not be the most popular framing for a chronicle.<br /> <br /> No, the last we heard about W5 had nothing to do with the Garou Nation fracturing, but more to do with them wanting to start a Second Impergium. Which is something COMPLETELY different then what's above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T23:37:40-08:00","id":1265705,"title":"","content":"Starting a Second Impergium? Ok, yeah, 1) that's gonna throw the Veil right out the window (the small scale Red Talon version of the Impergium notwithstanding) and 2) the Garou don't have anywhere near the numbers to pull that off now that humanity numbers above 7 billion people and 3) could very well result in a civil war in the Garou Nation because close to half the Tribes will fight against it, not the least of which will be the CoG, the Bone Gnawers, the Glass Walkers and the Black Furies because of their relatively close ties to humanity.<br /> <br /> Hmm, actually, trying to start the Second Impergium could be what leads to the Garou Nation fracturing after all.<br /> <br /> But I still don't like this idea. It seems like the 5th Editions of the oWoD are taking place in a world that couldn't plausibly pass for our world even though that exactly what the World of Darkness is supposed to be in theory. Could the Garou Nation conceivably carry out a Second Impergium <i>without humanity even noticing?</i> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ExtraStrengthMasquerade\" target=\"_blank\">Extra Strength Masquerade</a> indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T00:04:55-08:00","id":1265706,"title":"","content":"Now, the thing with the Second Impergium was at one of said conferences a year ago. Considering all the controversies surrounding V5 and the promise to change their developmental process, it's up in the air if that's still going to be a thing W5 or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T04:21:55-08:00","id":1265757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265633#post1265633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that's what they're doing. Not entirely, at least.<br /> <br /> BNS WtA had the whole thing about the Garou Nation splitting up into different factions. However, BNS has admitted that it's less to do with nuWW executive direction and more to do with adapting to a LARP. That because the type of gameplay of a LARP is completely different from a TRPG, that changes had to be made. In this case, that LARP is more suited to politicking gameplay, and WtA TRPG setting wasn't as suited to it the same way that Vampire and Changeling are. Apparently, moot politicking wasn't a good enough hook, and (from my time looking at WtA communities), that tends to not be the most popular framing for a chronicle.<br /> <br /> No, the last we heard about W5 had nothing to do with the Garou Nation fracturing, but more to do with them wanting to start a Second Impergium. Which is something COMPLETELY different then what's above.</div> </div> </div> </div>They still had the phrase &quot;Black Furies use the few homid males they have for breeding with their lupus kinfolk&quot; in the first published version of Changing Ways. In the BNS setting, Furies now accept males to their tribe, which is not canon in the 20th. Given how long Changing Ways was in production, this is a very recent addition to the book. It was fixed to 'black fury BLOODED male homids' after being corrected in the Errata thread. There is also a suggested disaster which makes the Gauntlet harder to cross (as it is in the BNS setting.)<br /> <br /> For the second Impegrium, I just roll my eyes at it. Because most tribes have homid kinfolk, there can always be kinfolk you don't know about. So Impegrium 2.0 is not very workable. Plus, the whole point of the setting is how the past wrongs are haunting the garou, Impegrium as one of the biggest ones.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T06:04:17-08:00","id":1265785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265757#post1265757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the second Impegrium, I just roll my eyes at it. Because most tribes have homid kinfolk, there can always be kinfolk you don't know about. So Impegrium 2.0 is not very workable. Plus, the whole point of the setting is how the past wrongs are haunting the garou, Impegrium as one of the biggest ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think so? I'd say that the biggest mistake that keeps returning in the Garou history is the War of Rage. The Impergium was stopped out of fear that it would have strengthened the Wyrm, but given how powerful the Weaver became and how much the human race ended up helping the Wyrm I think that a lot of Garou could conclude that the real mistake was stopping.<br /> <br /> Of course, without the War of Rage the fera would have helped keeping the balance and maybe the humans wouldn't have degenerated to such an extent (well, to be fair Shattered Dreams suggests that without the war of rage the Garou would have been too weak to face the Wyrm later on and that the current story is the best of the possible worlds, but I'm not sure I agree on that).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T07:44:37-08:00","id":1265819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265785#post1265785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think so? I'd say that the biggest mistake that keeps returning in the Garou history is the War of Rage. The Impergium was stopped out of fear that it would have strengthened the Wyrm, but given how powerful the Weaver became and how much the human race ended up helping the Wyrm I think that a lot of Garou could conclude that the real mistake was stopping.<br /> <br /> Of course, without the War of Rage the fera would have helped keeping the balance and maybe the humans wouldn't have degenerated to such an extent (well, to be fair Shattered Dreams suggests that without the war of rage the Garou would have been too weak to face the Wyrm later on and that the current story is the best of the possible worlds, but I'm not sure I agree on that).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Impegrium separated humans from Gaia in a very real way, the Delirium is the result of that. There can never be unity between garou and humans, since they have cemented in humanity's mind that they are monsters. Plus, the Impegrium was when the Nation truly split into separate tribes and the Litany was written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T16:29:23-08:00","id":1265975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265819#post1265819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Impegrium separated humans from Gaia in a very real way, the Delirium is the result of that. There can never be unity between garou and humans, since they have cemented in humanity's mind that they are monsters. Plus, the Impegrium was when the Nation truly split into separate tribes and the Litany was written.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. One has to remember that one of the main themes of W:tA is that one of the largest reasons that the Garou are losing the war against the Wyrm is that the Garou of ancient times screwed up too badly in the past for the Garou of the End Times to win. Ethan Skemp, one of the old developers for W:tA, even mentioned something like this in his Afterthoughts essay in the 2nd Ed. Werewolf Player's Guide (see &quot;Blind faith is bad&quot;on page 214 if you want to read it yourself). The Impergium resulted in the Curse alienating the Garou from humanity. The War of Tears resulted in an entire tribe of Garou being exterminated at the claws of their kin. The War(s) of Rage and the War of Shame drove the other Changing Breeds to (or even past) the brink of extinction, depriving Gaia of many of her much-needed defenders. Every single time the Garou let their Rage and pride get the better of them, they (and Gaia) paid a <i>very</i> heavy price for it. The Garou didn't get off scot-free once. <i>Not. Even. Once.</i> And some Garou, the Shadow Lords and the Red Talons not least among them, <i>still</i> think that <i>stopping</i> the Impergium was the Garou's greatest mistake, rather than starting it in the first place. This shows that some among the Garou still haven't learned the right lessons: that sometimes clawing the shit out of something is counterproductive in the war against the Wyrm and that the Garou become their own worst enemies if they keep letting their Rage get the better of them.<br /> <br /> Hell, it can be argued that the Garou <i>have already become</i> their own worst enemies centuries ago and <i>it's too late to save the world</i> because of that. How do you as a player and as a character react in that case? Do you let yourself fall into Harano or do you get up and fight because your duty to Gaia won't let you lie down and die? Or, as in the case of far too many Garou who decided that winning was more important than standing up for a cause, do you decide to join the ranks of the Enemy?<br /> <br /> How will you deal with the fuckups of your ancestors? Will you try to make up for them? And if you try, do you even have a chance of succeeding? And if not, what then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T16:35:13-08:00","id":1265982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265633#post1265633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that's what they're doing. Not entirely, at least.<br /> <br /> BNS WtA had the whole thing about the Garou Nation splitting up into different factions. However, BNS has admitted that it's less to do with nuWW executive direction and more to do with adapting to a LARP. That because the type of gameplay of a LARP is completely different from a TRPG, that changes had to be made. In this case, that LARP is more suited to politicking gameplay, and WtA TRPG setting wasn't as suited to it the same way that Vampire and Changeling are. Apparently, moot politicking wasn't a good enough hook, and (from my time looking at WtA communities), that tends to not be the most popular framing for a chronicle.<br /> <br /> No, the last we heard about W5 had nothing to do with the Garou Nation fracturing, but more to do with them wanting to start a Second Impergium. Which is something COMPLETELY different then what's above.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As someone who werewolf larps cutting your politicing options from 13 to 7 doesn't make things more political. BNS is all sorts of a mess it comes off as something a Vampire larper decided would &quot;Fix&quot; Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T07:11:48-08:00","id":1266399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265463#post1265463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> NuWW de-canoned Shattered Dreams.....screwed with Changing Ways.....got TB Bunyip cancelled......I mean after reading and playing V5 they were pushing shit uphill to make me give them a chance but they're doing they're best to actively piss WtA fans off. But I guess if they're looking at basing it on the stuff they signed off on for BNS WtA we're all gonna be pissed off anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>... just when I was startign to forget that clusterfuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T07:23:14-08:00","id":1266401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265982#post1265982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As someone who werewolf larps cutting your politicing options from 13 to 7 doesn't make things more political. BNS is all sorts of a mess it comes off as something a Vampire larper decided would &quot;Fix&quot; Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add to it that now Fera can officially join in packs among Sanctum of Gaia. Mind, THAT I do not mind. But the rewriting of Black Furies, Glass Walkers, Red Talons,etc. is the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T22:05:07-08:00","id":1266864,"title":"","content":"In my opinion Impegrium in some tribes point of view was natural. My favourite tribebook - Red Talons revised explained exactly why it was so important. All the mythology and devotion so different from other tribes and the point in history where they are now are strictly connected to impegrium. I agree with Shadow Lord point of wiev that Talons are heart of tribes. The biggest tragedy is that the main talons question is unanswered by so called leaders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T22:33:53-08:00","id":1266869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1266401#post1266401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Add to it that now Fera can officially join in packs among Sanctum of Gaia. Mind, THAT I do not mind. But the rewriting of Black Furies, Glass Walkers, Red Talons,etc. is the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So basically they took off a bunch of tribes and decided &quot;hey no one is going to play this&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T22:35:03-08:00","id":1266870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265982#post1265982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As someone who werewolf larps cutting your politicing options from 13 to 7 doesn't make things more political. BNS is all sorts of a mess it comes off as something a Vampire larper decided would &quot;Fix&quot; Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>An <b>abomination</b> of a game, if one would...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T23:13:35-08:00","id":1266880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1266869#post1266869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So basically they took off a bunch of tribes and decided &quot;hey no one is going to play this&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>More like &quot;These guys are TRADITIONALISTS! and THESE guys are PROGRESSIVES!....but they can still pack up.&quot; Then they messed up the Talons because OBVIOUSLY they would just ally with a faction torturing humans to feed the land all wyrmy way. When previously that camp had been a secret society for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1266864#post1266864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion Impegrium in some tribes point of view was natural. My favourite tribebook - Red Talons revised explained exactly why it was so important. All the mythology and devotion so different from other tribes and the point in history where they are now are strictly connected to impegrium. I agree with Shadow Lord point of wiev that Talons are heart of tribes. The biggest tragedy is that the main talons question is unanswered by so called leaders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not to get political, but the Talons could have loped to the Litany meeting to get answers. Instead they refused since it was 'too human' and now they bitch and moan no one asked -them- how the Litany should go.<br /> <br /> I love the Talons, but they do put fingers in their ears a lot in order to keep living as close to wolves as they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 11-13-2018, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T11:13:42-08:00","id":1267019,"title":"","content":"Talons were forced to become a tribe. They don't understand many things including politics. They follow simple rules that don't fit for humanity. Reading the tribebook I've learned about WtA more then ever I guess. I think that they know at the primal level that their creator is dying and with that they as creation would dissapear. And they found the guilty in humanity. In my opinion the book of Weaver confirmed that. I.think that the book of Weaver is much more adult then it seems. Humanity is Weaver tribe. It's game of war. Talons are loosing it. Weaver plays dirty and Talons don't have the big spectrum of view on that. They have a weapon that was working - impegrium. Other tribes stole the weapon away. Talons become defenceless. So they want to go back to ways that was working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T19:13:39-08:00","id":1267172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267019#post1267019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talons were forced to become a tribe. They don't understand many things including politics. They follow simple rules that don't fit for humanity. Reading the tribebook I've learned about WtA more then ever I guess. I think that they know at the primal level that their creator is dying and with that they as creation would dissapear. And they found the guilty in humanity. In my opinion the book of Weaver confirmed that. I.think that the book of Weaver is much more adult then it seems. Humanity is Weaver tribe. It's game of war. Talons are loosing it. Weaver plays dirty and Talons don't have the big spectrum of view on that. They have a weapon that was working - impegrium. Other tribes stole the weapon away. Talons become defenceless. So they want to go back to ways that was working.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were forced to become a tribe, because they refused to make their case known. Despite living like wolves, Talons are very much as intelligent as humans. This is what I like about them, despite their obvious issues, they very much caused many of those by denial. Like the Litany, they were summoned, they thought it was too human. What happened was that, like in all wolf packs, the majority won.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T19:41:31-08:00","id":1267178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267019#post1267019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talons were forced to become a tribe. They don't understand many things including politics. They follow simple rules that don't fit for humanity. Reading the tribebook I've learned about WtA more then ever I guess. I think that they know at the primal level that their creator is dying and with that they as creation would dissapear. And they found the guilty in humanity. In my opinion the book of Weaver confirmed that. I.think that the book of Weaver is much more adult then it seems. Humanity is Weaver tribe. It's game of war. Talons are loosing it. Weaver plays dirty and Talons don't have the big spectrum of view on that. They have a weapon that was working - impegrium. Other tribes stole the weapon away. Talons become defenceless. So they want to go back to ways that was working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Gaia gave that job to someone else. The Imperigum was always second guessing Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T23:17:11-08:00","id":1267203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267178#post1267178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except Gaia gave that job to someone else. The Imperigum was always second guessing Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>To who? Please remind me. I forgot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T08:12:51-08:00","id":1267295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267203#post1267203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To who? Please remind me. I forgot</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ratkin were created to spread disease and eat food stores in order to keep the human population in check. The Garou decimated them during the War of Rage and the human population exploded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T09:38:50-08:00","id":1267332,"title":"","content":"Thank you for reminding me! Shit, honestly, I missed that uterly. And while that changes a lot, still keeping the human population in check by impegrium was some kind of solution. Besides garou as I remember didn't bother about other fera duties cause of puting themselves on the top of Gaia's chosen - by being her defenders. I always played WtA almost without fera cause it's game about werewolves after all.As always it's a point of view and world created by gm is his chosen option. <br /> Sorry for blurring the main topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T18:39:56-08:00","id":1267472,"title":"","content":"Back to the topic, as funny as the &quot;SJWs in VAMPIRE!?!&quot; videos are, I find it very interesting how much of nuWW is focusing on making choices that are very edgy compared to the 20th editions.<br /> <br /> As for why I am such a gun-ho 'no cismen in Furies' proponent, it has to do with the the roles each tribe plays in the game. A Fenrir, a Fianna and a Wendigo are all from warrior tribes, but they cannot be compared to one another by how they act/their culture. It is to make playing them clearer and easier. Furies, if they accept men, end up basically as far more angry Children of Gaia. It is already common for Fury characters to be very close to Coggie characters in their goals/way of life/etc.<br /> <br /> Plus, just the reality that Furies were never meant to fight for equality. They fought for the rights of women, because they were tasked to it by Luna. Their homeland is in Greece, which historically had a pretty pathriarcial culture. They are are not a tribe of calm and peace like Children of Gaia, they very much can be utterly brutal with their rites.If you take away the reason why they exist by making them accept cismen, it erases what makes the furies unique in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T20:03:55-08:00","id":1267490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267332#post1267332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for reminding me! Shit, honestly, I missed that uterly. And while that changes a lot, still keeping the human population in check by impegrium was some kind of solution. Besides garou as I remember didn't bother about other fera duties cause of puting themselves on the top of Gaia's chosen - by being her defenders. I always played WtA almost without fera cause it's game about werewolves after all.As always it's a point of view and world created by gm is his chosen option.<br /> Sorry for blurring the main topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>No that's intrinsically the issue. The Garou decided they could to everyone elses job better, which was always second guessing Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T22:38:16-08:00","id":1267509,"title":"","content":"Wasn't the fault of starting the first (?) war of rage belong to Silver Fangs? Not every tribe? <br /> <br /> Besides thinking about 5th edition there are several questions on my mind:<br /> <br /> 1) is there a leader of garou nation?<br /> 2) what's the status of tribes septs caerns and camps<br /> 3) are there any umbral quests active? What happened to umbra? Is the spirit world changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T05:41:05-08:00","id":1267556,"title":"","content":"Short question: anyone here think also that they will be largely streamlining the game and setting? Meaning that we'll probably only get a limited scope of possibly 7 tribes for the initital corebook? If so, what are your bets for Tribes to definitely be included?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <br /> also: Mummy the Curse<br /> I buy all other books usually on DriveThruRPG.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2477-zydake","name":"zydake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2477_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T07:11:53-08:00","id":1267568,"title":"","content":"Hope not. While dividing clans to various books like anarch and camarilla is ... natural? That the core WtA.always had all tribes. But I am deeply afraid that they would divide it in 3 section - neutral Striders, stars and sanctum acording to MET plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T08:06:51-08:00","id":1267577,"title":"","content":"Which MET book divided the tribes? I've been leafing through Laws of the Apocalypse, Laws of the Wyld and Laws of the Wyld revised, and I'm missing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T08:18:16-08:00","id":1267581,"title":"","content":"By Night Studio. My mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T08:22:31-08:00","id":1267582,"title":"","content":"My theory for Werewolf fuel and abilities is that RAGE will function like HUNGER in V5 (suggested . Risking an increase of Rage die would be done to ignore damage impairments, to change form more rapidly, and activate some gifts. I'm betting that other gifts would reduce RAGE (the gifts that were fueled more by Gnosis in previous editions), making various gifts and powers be a part of an ever changing economy of RAGE and power. Going into War Form willingly would also eat up RAGE i'd imagine, while reaching RAGE 5 would force a War Form Frenzy much like HUNGER 5 would do to a vampire, but use up at least 1 RAGE before calming and returning to another form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T09:36:16-08:00","id":1267598,"title":"","content":"I guess You're right about rage stuff and it hurt my eyes. While it is hard to swallow for me I can accept if the gifts and rites.would be well build and combat would be quicker without use of advices like max 3 rounds of fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T11:49:15-08:00","id":1267636,"title":"","content":"Combats drag on for that long because the combat system requires too many dice rolls. Roll 10 for attack, roll 9 for defense, roll 14 for damage, roll 8 to soak, here remove 3 damage from the 24 Essence pool of that spirit. Now it's his turn. Repeat until the remaining 21 points are depleted.<br /> <br /> In comparison, a regular action requires just an extended opposed roll, tops. If they handled fights with extended rolls they might end up being slimmer, but still at risk of deadlocks (= lot of rounds without anyone wounding anyone). Exalted puts a minimum of 1 die of damage after soaking if I remember, that alone might be enough to put a better time limit to the fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T10:25:40-08:00","id":1267905,"title":"","content":"So with this announcement I wonder what will happen with <a href=\"https://www.white-wolf.com/newsblog/a-message-from-white-wolf\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.white-wolf.com/newsblog/...rom-white-wolf</a> I wonder if they will outsource W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T10:51:58-08:00","id":1267920,"title":"","content":"Soo, let's all welcome censure in the White Wolf products! \\o/<br /> /sarcasticmode off","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T10:52:52-08:00","id":1267923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267905#post1267905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with this announcement I wonder what will happen with <a href=\"https://www.white-wolf.com/newsblog/a-message-from-white-wolf\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.white-wolf.com/newsblog/...rom-white-wolf</a> I wonder if they will outsource W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the chickens have come home to roost, more like it. NuWW made their choices and showed poor judgement, which caused fan uproar that was justified. Chenya being misused was most likely the last straw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267920#post1267920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soo, let's all welcome censure in the White Wolf products! \\o/<br /> /sarcasticmode off</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between censorship of anything dark and avoiding topics which are very raw to a lot of real people who went through a horrible war/genocide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 11-16-2018, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T11:33:17-08:00","id":1267933,"title":"","content":"Company was kicked by the fandom. The main target group for their games. Evil. Wyrm would be proud. F..k that , if W20.would be continued.I.be glad. Just give me Rage.lcg and.I.can live with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T11:43:09-08:00","id":1267939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267923#post1267923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference between censorship of anything dark and avoiding topics which are very raw to a lot of real people who went through a horrible war/genocide.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not particularly relevant for the issue at hand though. Their screw-up triggered the Power That Be that from now on will take care of sanitizing the new material, and whatever may happen from now on there's a freedom loss that's here to stay. No author in the WW will ever be able to touch anything that a person with the only purpose in life to avoid any kind of lawsuit or inconvenience for the company is going to evaluate as &quot;sensitive&quot;.<br /> <br /> The 9/11 was used as an excuse for the US government to violate the citizens' privacy and implement limits that 17years later still are in place. There's the chance that Paradox Interactive is going to use their vigilance in a better way, but I'm not really hopeful.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong. We'll see with the next books I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T12:21:59-08:00","id":1267957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267923#post1267923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the chickens have come home to roost, more like it. NuWW made their choices and showed poor judgement, which caused fan uproar that was justified. Chenya being misused was most likely the last straw.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has nothing to do with my question which was do people think they will outsource W5 or finish it in house?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T12:30:47-08:00","id":1267967,"title":"","content":"I wish W20 would be official 5ed or 5ed would be made by team that made W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T12:34:31-08:00","id":1267970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267939#post1267939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not particularly relevant for the issue at hand though. Their screw-up triggered the Power That Be that from now on will take care of sanitizing the new material, and whatever may happen from now on there's a freedom loss that's here to stay. No author in the WW will ever be able to touch anything that a person with the only purpose in life to avoid any kind of lawsuit or inconvenience for the company is going to evaluate as &quot;sensitive&quot;.<br /> <br /> The 9/11 was used as an excuse for the US government to violate the citizens' privacy and implement limits that 17years later still are in place. There's the chance that Paradox Interactive is going to use their vigilance in a better way, but I'm not really hopeful.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong. We'll see with the next books I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume there wasn't oversight to begin with. Paradox knew what it bought, the company that had written Shoah and such serious books. I don't think they are sanitizing the future WoD books, rather they will take more care in hiring people.<br /> <br /> I mean, they wouldn't restructure the entire staff if it was just that one mistake with Chenya. It was just the last straw of the messes the nuWW had done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267957#post1267957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has nothing to do with my question which was do people think they will outsource W5 or finish it in house?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they will either source it to Onyx Path or do it in house. I don't think they'd outsource it entirely, given its importance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T13:44:32-08:00","id":1268024,"title":"","content":"A whole bunch of nuWW fans are now saying that the plan all along was for them to only publish V5 and the Camarilla and Anarch books with everything else to be outsourced ( including Sabbat?)....if thats the case ( which I don't really believe) then nothing has changed at all and W5 was always going to be outsourced.<br /> <br /> Or maybe V5 can just be considered a one-off variant game and OPP can plug on with their own plans for everything OWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 11-16-2018, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T14:34:45-08:00","id":1268047,"title":"","content":"One should consider that there is even more then the recent controversy here... It's been almost three years since Paradox had founded the White Wolf Publishing company to show off and capitalise on their new shiny IP. What do they have to show three years later?<ul><li><div align=\"left\">Betting machines</div></li> <li><div align=\"left\">Two mediocre visual novels, one of which stirred a hornet's nest with its creepy shit</div></li> <li><div align=\"left\">The most controversial edition of Vampire</div></li> <li><div align=\"left\">A vapourware Werewolf computer game</div></li> <li><div align=\"left\">... and a line of Vampire lipsticks</div></li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 11-16-2018, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T15:04:16-08:00","id":1268056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268047#post1268047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><div align=\"left\">A vapourware Werewolf computer game</div></li> </ul><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... that is the WtA Legacy. VtM had two games, WtA TRIED to have 2 games, failed at both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T16:29:27-08:00","id":1268090,"title":"","content":"The WtA video game is still under development. It IS coming. It IS real. As for whether or not it will be good, remains to be seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T19:06:10-08:00","id":1268122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;White Wolf will no longer develop and publish these products internally. This has always been the intended goal for White Wolf as a company, and it is now time to enact it.&quot; </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.white-wolf.com/newsblog/a-message-from-white-wolf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.white-wolf.com/newsblog/a-message-from-white-wolf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.white-wolf.com/newsblog/a-message-from-white-wolf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.white-wolf.com/newsblog/a-message-from-white-wolf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I knew that was the case for all sorts of licensed goods, but I thought they'd always planned to at least do the TTRPG books in-house.<br /> But maybe they just wanted to get the fundamentals down and then have other companies continue the work they'd started---thus OPP's &quot;Chicago by Night&quot; is just the first book as they take over the license for TTRPG books from White Wolf?<br /> <br /> So, maybe OPP will indeed be &quot;in charge&quot; of continuing and creating W5, along with everything else of NuWW TTRPGs from here out? White Wolf will oversee and direct, but won't be producing the products themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T19:32:38-08:00","id":1268130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267970#post1267970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You assume there wasn't oversight to begin with. Paradox knew what it bought, the company that had written Shoah and such serious books. I don't think they are sanitizing the future WoD books, rather they will take more care in hiring people.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying it's a foreboding decision even if taken in good faith.<br /> I mean, it's not like I fully appreciated nuWW products, I in fact openly criticized some of the ideas they were pushing. Still, Joriani's post feels insincere and is conveying a troubling subtext, so let's say I'm staying wary for a while and wait for their next prints before judging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The WtA video game is still under development. It IS coming. It IS real. As for whether or not it will be good, remains to be seen. </div> </div> </div>Yet, it was announced about three years ago and there's nothing about it. Not a trailer, not a website, not a devblog. When Obsidian begun with Pillars of Eternity they kept a regular newsletter to keep every backer updated on the development, and even when they had nothing to show (because they were coding the engine) they still offered concept art, breakdown of the playable classes and some insight on the setting.<br /> <br /> The WtA game begins to look a lot more like Cyberpunk, that had CD project red lying on its progress while they blocked its development to redirect every effort on the 8-months-late Witcher 3, resuming it only after relasing the expansion pack. I'd say that it's clear at this point that they are not showing anything because there's nothing to show: WtA game was expected for 2018 and we don't even have a gameplay video, meaning that it's coming for 2019 christmas <u>at best</u>, more likely 2020 (if it's coming at all).<br /> <br /> Let's just hope it's going to be a Cyberpunk and not a Duke Nukem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T19:44:32-08:00","id":1268132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267939#post1267939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not particularly relevant for the issue at hand though. Their screw-up triggered the Power That Be that from now on will take care of sanitizing the new material, and whatever may happen from now on there's a freedom loss that's here to stay. No author in the WW will ever be able to touch anything that a person with the only purpose in life to avoid any kind of lawsuit or inconvenience for the company is going to evaluate as &amp;quot;sensitive&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> The 9/11 was used as an excuse for the US government to violate the citizens' privacy and implement limits that 17years later still are in place. There's the chance that Paradox Interactive is going to use their vigilance in a better way, but I'm not really hopeful.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong. We'll see with the next books I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t take complaints of \u201cfreedom loss\u201d seriously when nWW was using its editorial oversight to change the content of OPP published 20th Anniversary supplements to push an (outdated) \u201cedgy\u201d setting aesthetic. Their bosses exercising editorial oversight on them is not new entry of censorship into the system. Editorial oversight is part of professional publishing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T19:50:42-08:00","id":1268134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1267923#post1267923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the chickens have come home to roost, more like it. NuWW made their choices and showed poor judgement, which caused fan uproar that was justified. Chenya being misused was most likely the last straw.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is a difference between censorship of anything dark and avoiding topics which are very raw to a lot of real people who went through a horrible war/genocide.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m open to real and raw issues getting mature discussion and exploration. The evils Garou fight in-setting depend on being able to do that in fact. But \u201cthis real world ongoing horrific evil affecting a marginalized community with a higher than average overlap with our readership, is just a decoy created by vampires from made up even worse stuff\u201d is emphatically NOT \u201cmature discussion and exploration\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T20:31:54-08:00","id":1268144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268132#post1268132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can\u2019t take complaints of \u201cfreedom loss\u201d seriously when nWW was using its editorial oversight to change the content of OPP published 20th Anniversary supplements to push an (outdated) \u201cedgy\u201d setting aesthetic. Their bosses exercising editorial oversight on them is not new entry of censorship into the system. Editorial oversight is part of professional publishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're however missing how the point is not how justified may look now but what is this going to imply in the long term.<br /> As long as editorial oversight means quality check I have no complains. Pretty sure they already had one, btw, even if he wasn't doing a great job. Right now, though, it's a political answer pandering to a part of the fanbase and aimed to keep Paradox away from a certain kind of notoriety.<br /> <br /> You didn't like nWW products, I didn't either (some of them, at least - shattered dreams was quite good IMHO), still I'm expecting them to become worse now. So, if you don't mind, I'll keep my expectations low for a while and give these guys a chance to prove me wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T20:37:04-08:00","id":1268146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268144#post1268144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're however missing how the point is not how justified may look now but what is this going to imply in the long term.<br /> As long as editorial oversight means quality check I have no complains. Pretty sure they already had one, btw, even if he wasn't doing a great job. Right now, though, it's a political answer pandering to a part of the fanbase and aimed to keep Paradox away from a certain kind of notoriety.<br /> <br /> You didn't like nWW products, I didn't either (some of them, at least - shattered dreams was quite good IMHO), still I'm expecting them to become worse now. So, if you don't mind, I'll keep my expectations low for a while and give these guys a chance to prove me wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is political only in the sense that insulting real people by implying -vampires- caused a genocide, or a peadophile vampire as a playtest pc or any other mess is. Yes, it is a statement of viewpoints, but I'd say it is less pandering and more 'hey, we have seen you guys cannot handle yourselves properly'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T21:01:08-08:00","id":1268151,"title":"","content":"Uh...Shattered Dreams is OPP, all NuWW did was stick a sidebar in saying ' non-canon' after it was written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:23:31-08:00","id":1268170,"title":"","content":"Just get email response and I'm little more optimistic about Werewolf 5th edition. It shouldn't be toned down with theme and colorfull pretty game. And WW will ask OPP for assiatance in making the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:36:36-08:00","id":1268175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268146#post1268146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is political only in the sense that insulting real people by implying -vampires- caused a genocide.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is only insulting if you can't split fiction from reality. WW has always given supernatural context for tragic events like World War 2, native American massacres, Amazonian deforestation and the destruction of Pompei. W20 defined the Greek economic crysis as a work of the Wyrm and after five years there's score of people there that still scrape to reach the end of the month.<br /> And this is only what I can conjure on the spot, pretty sure that if I had the time I could dig out as many examples I wish. So, what's so different this time that you need to feel outraged?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Uh...Shattered Dreams is OPP, all NuWW did was stick a sidebar in saying ' non-canon' after it was written. </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry then. I'm getting an hard time remembering it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:37:48-08:00","id":1268176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268151#post1268151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh...Shattered Dreams is OPP, all NuWW did was stick a sidebar in saying ' non-canon' after it was written.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 Changing Ways, on the other hand, had multiple additions and changes not made to it by WW that are not obvious to the reader as being so, against the wishes of the book's developer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:47:05-08:00","id":1268177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268175#post1268175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is only insulting if you can't split fiction from reality. WW has always given supernatural context for tragic events like World War 2, native American massacres, Amazonian deforestation and the destruction of Pompei. W20 defined the Greek economic crysis as a work of the Wyrm and after five years there's score of people there that still scrape to reach the end of the month.<br /> And this is only what I can conjure on the spot, pretty sure that if I had the time I could dig out as many examples I wish. So, what's so different this time that you need to feel outraged?</div> </div> </div> </div>Using real world human evil as a setting element that impacts the supernatural. Fine!<br /> <br /> Using the supernatural as an extended metaphor for real world human evils (see Wyrm stuff). Trickier, but if you can pull it off, great!<br /> <br /> Dismissing real world ONGOING human evils as a distraction meant to deflect from the actually serious made up stuff in your game - NOT OK!<br /> <br /> <br /> Clear on the difference now?<br /> <br /> And fiction matters directly reflects and impacts the social attitudes in the world it exists in - it matters. MLK told Michele Nichols she couldn\u2019t quit Star Trek for a damn good reason after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-17-2018, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:57:38-08:00","id":1268179,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m really not worried about the company that makes the Europa Universalis games becoming \u201clets censor history so we don\u2019t upset anybody\u201d happy. They actively pride themselves on engaging with real world atrocities in a form that properly contextualizes them. This was off-brand for them, and they responded in that spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T23:09:04-08:00","id":1268181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268176#post1268176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 Changing Ways, on the other hand, had multiple additions and changes not made to it by WW that are not obvious to the reader as being so, against the wishes of the book's developer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, yes. Just making clear that it was still an OPP product not a NuWW one.<br /> <br /> The only books by NuWW are V5 Core, Anarchs, Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 11-17-2018, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T00:23:54-08:00","id":1268194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268179#post1268179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m really not worried about the company that makes the Europa Universalis games becoming \u201clets censor history so we don\u2019t upset anybody\u201d happy. They actively pride themselves on engaging with real world atrocities in a form that properly contextualizes them. This was off-brand for them, and they responded in that spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>AND Crusader Kings I&amp;II and Mount and Blade and its sequels. This is not a company that is very squeamish about topics. This is why I was happy -Paradox- took on World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Which is why the nuWW was such a disappointment for me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T03:59:38-08:00","id":1268222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268130#post1268130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yet, <b>it was announced about three years ago</b> and there's nothing about it. Not a trailer, not a website, not a devblog.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It was announced January of 2017. That was LESS THAN TWO YEARS AGO. <br /> <br /> They have a website for the game. They even have forums, too. Crazy, I know!<br /> <br /> They have shown a bunch of concept art. <br /> <br /> The main man at Paradox just confirmed it's coming.<br /> <br /> Games take a long time to develop, so I'm not sure what more do you want in a year and a half of game development.<br /> <br /> <br /> Listen, I don't give a shit whether you think it's coming or not, but at least state facts. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T05:18:48-08:00","id":1268232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268222#post1268222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was announced January of 2017. That was LESS THAN TWO YEARS AGO.<br /> <br /> They have a website for the game. They even have forums, too. Crazy, I know!<br /> <br /> They have shown a bunch of concept art.<br /> <br /> The main man at Paradox just confirmed it's coming.<br /> <br /> Games take a long time to develop, so I'm not sure what more do you want in a year and a half of game development.<br /> <br /> <br /> Listen, I don't give a shit whether you think it's coming or not, but at least state facts. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've stated that it's vapourware. Not that it's never coming out.<br /> <br /> - announcement almost two years ago means that it has been in production for longer then that<br /> - they have a design element for forums on their webpage that does not work<br /> - bunch of concept art is generous for what they have actually shown<br /> - what the guy in Paradox knows is that it's licensed and that the publisher has paid their dues and that they did not contravene any deadlines agreed upon by the former WW team, that doesn't mean he has direct oversight of the production or that the old WW crew did. Neither is it a commitment to it coming out in 2018 as was announced.<br /> <br /> What we do know on the other hand is telling;<br /> - there is no mention of anything technical for the game - engine, mechanics, systems, not even platforms or what order they plan to come out on<br /> - the demonstrations are all interviews with the faces of the dev team who are offering hype and general statments<br /> - the industry presence is distinctly meant for journalists<br /> - the journalists aren't taking it very seriously<br /> - Cyanide is a small team and all their efforts have been on the big push for Call of Cthulhu<br /> - the marketing cycle for CoC started almost a year ago with demos, images and hype from chaosium and the devs<br /> <br /> The game was scheduled for 2018, and from everything we've seen and the low effort they've made for marketing the game won't be out for at least a year and a half, if not more. Therefore there is nothing substantial there, therefore it qualifies pretty well as vapourware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 11-17-2018, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T06:06:53-08:00","id":1268243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268177#post1268177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clear on the difference now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me rephrase this.<br /> I'm clear on what triggers you. I just can't understand why and the reason you bring feels quite arbitrary to me.<br /> I don't feel outraged by what they wrote on Chechnya. I may consider it cheap but that's not enough to offend me. I don't feel outraged by the existence of a pedophile vampire (and even here, it's not like she was openly declared a pedophile IIRC, she just had that feel), we have a setting in which the people gets, literally, dismembered to be remodeled in living, thinking chairs and a pedophile just barely qualifies to be in the same league.<br /> <br /> You felt offended by all this, that's fine. But I didn't and a lot of other people didn't either, I can't force myself to feel something I don't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Listen, I don't give a shit whether you think it's coming or not, but at least state facts. Thanks. </div> </div> </div>Wanna hear facts? The website is still exactly the same of January 2017. No images, no descriptions, just a Crinos zoomed in. The &quot;devblog&quot; area is inactive and half of the clickable buttons do not work, as if no one ever thought about finishing the webpage; overall there's not a single useful information to get from that place. The facebook page is abandoned and that's pretty much what happened to their other social media. No forum has ever been linked on the official web page, or none I could find. Paradox has no section for Werewolf among the &quot;upcoming games&quot; in their forum, the Cyanide website only offers a few lines about the game plot that are not updated since two years ago. Focus Home interactive does have a werewolf forum, with exactly 23 topics inside (in two years!) mostly made by unanswered questions for the devs.<br /> <br /> You say it's coming? Great, because I really want it to. They're just not really behaving as it's going to.<br /> In the exact same time frame the Obsidians had really a lot to show for their work, so at least I believe this means they're very behind schedule with the coding. Perhaps in the next E3 Cyanide is going to surprise everyone with videos and official trailers, but for the time being the only thing I have are their (few) words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T08:20:02-08:00","id":1268280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268232#post1268232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've stated that it's vapourware. Not that it's never coming out.<br /> <br /> - announcement almost two years ago means that it has been in production for longer then that<br /> - they have a design element for forums on their webpage that does not work<br /> - bunch of concept art is generous for what they have actually shown<br /> - what the guy in Paradox knows is that it's licensed and that the publisher has paid their dues and that they did not contravene any deadlines agreed upon by the former WW team, that doesn't mean he has direct oversight of the production or that the old WW crew did. Neither is it a commitment to it coming out in 2018 as was announced.<br /> <br /> What we do know on the other hand is telling;<br /> - there is no mention of anything technical for the game - engine, mechanics, systems, not even platforms or what order they plan to come out on<br /> - the demonstrations are all interviews with the faces of the dev team who are offering hype and general statments<br /> - the industry presence is distinctly meant for journalists<br /> - the journalists aren't taking it very seriously<br /> - Cyanide is a small team and all their efforts have been on the big push for Call of Cthulhu<br /> - the marketing cycle for CoC started almost a year ago with demos, images and hype from chaosium and the devs<br /> <br /> The game was scheduled for 2018, and from everything we've seen and the low effort they've made for marketing the game won't be out for at least a year and a half, if not more. Therefore there is nothing substantial there, therefore it qualifies pretty well as vapourware.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay. Cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T21:34:17-08:00","id":1268476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265380#post1265380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1/ So having an utterly remorseless enemy consisting of an entire third of the fabric of reality itself is not scary enough for you? An enemy of which only a small part of its army consists of utterly insane werewolves who represent everything you could become if you lose yourself too much to your Rage? An enemy capable of turning you into one of them if they capture you and make you dance the Black Spiral if they don't torture you to death first? An enemy that is winning the war to <i>decide the fate of the universe</i> despite all your best efforts? All this by you isn't scary?<br /> <br /> 2/ &quot;Less whining?&quot; You're talking about &quot;less whining&quot; when the Garou's morale in fighting a war to save the world is at (and in the case of Garou suffering under Harano, even past) the breaking point? Losing a war is <i>supposed</i> to be depressing precisely because of all the things that are at stake. As for &quot;making some enemies that can actually kill a pack of werewolves,&quot; did you forget about the aforementioned Black Spiral Dancers? Did you forget about the BSDs and Pentex's First Teams that have actually attacked and destroyed Garou septs, taken Garou caerns and converted them to Wyrmholes and Pits? Did you forget the minions of the Weaver who are almost as dangerous as the Wyrm? Did you forget that the last member of the Triat, the Wyld, can't even be counted as an ally precisely because its chaotic nature is so dangerous? Banes, formori, BSDs, and FRICKIN' NEXUS CRAWLERS aren't sufficiently dangerous to kill a werewolf pack? Seriously?<br /> <br /> 3/ &quot;Make going into rage a real danger.&quot; Succumbing to Rage isn't dangerous enough with the threat of falling into the Thrall of the Wyrm? Of losing control so thoroughly that you fall to cannibalism, rape or being unable to tell the difference between allies and enemies as you lose your literal self to a red haze of madness? This by you isn't dangerous?<br /> <br /> 4/ If you want problems that can't be solved just by ripping it to shreds, what about the afore-mentioned Pentex and all the industries it's corrupted and all the politicians it's bought or sidelined? You can't kill them without endangering the Veil. And even if you did manage to keep the Veil intact after killing the captains of industry or holders of political office, what then? The people you killed will just get replaced. There's a reason that Pentex is known as the Hydra. Did you forget the short story in W20 Book of the Wyrm where the Glass Walker kills everyone in a Pentex board room and the last Pentex guy standing blows cigar smoke into the Garou's face and says &quot;All this aftermath from a terrorist attack is just going to make our stock <i>rise</i>&quot;? The idea of how to fight a polluting corporation without resorting to ecoterrorism and creating a backlash that defeats the Garou anyway has been one of W:tA's main themes since Pentex was first introduced waaaaay back in the original Book of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> /5 Not enough tribe vs tribe conflict? Let's take a close look at that, shall we? The Black Furies and the Get of Fenris hate each other. The Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs are at odds over leading the Garou Nation. The Wendigo and Uktena are still upset with the European tribes (especially the Fianna, Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs) for taking their caerns and slaughtering their Kin during America's Manifest Destiny period. The Bone Gnawers are looked down upon by <i>almost all</i> the other Tribes (except the Glass Walkers and CoG) for being mongrels. The Red Talons hate all the other tribes for even having human kinfolk and REALLY hate the Glass Walkers for being influenced by the Weaver and living in cities. The theme that the Garou have always been at odds with each other and can't team up effectively to save Gaia has been there ever since 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> maryshelly, everything you're looking for in Werewolf has been there from the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>This here, though found in the first page of this thread, is very much something I'd like to bring attention to.<br /> <br /> I have stated multiple times before my motto for WtA games, but it bears repeating here; &quot;WtA has been played for 20 years by people around the world, the way you see the setting is not universal&quot;<br /> <br /> This goes into the above great post. The setting has these elements already, the problem is that the STs might not use them. In a game as huge as WtA, you can end up seeing it a very different light, if the one running the game does not enforce the setting. Mind, this isn't a 'STs are at fault' thing. Rather, the setting IS vast and it IS hard to really know how to do thing right.<br /> <br /> This is something a new edition for WtA needs, something to showcase the themes clearer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T06:55:35-08:00","id":1268538,"title":"","content":"Double post, but I figured this needed its own post;<br /> <br /> The biggest hurdle WtA suffers from, compared to Vampire, is that learning the setting takes way longer. This is because WtA isn't exactly what it says on the tin. As I have stated before, garou are more a fantasy race than traditional werewolves. I have done my best to study the myths for non-WtA projects, and garou really aren't what one expects when you pick up the game called werewolf. In contrast, though VtM gets silly as all hell, in general you are still playing the expected type of vampire. You can also play vampire without getting too deep into the lore, which in WtA is pretty...well, impossible.<br /> <br /> Of course, the fix shouldn't be to make WtA darker or more brutal. It already is those things. The problem is that WtA setting is fine as it is, but it isn't going to attract many werewolf-fans with the garou being what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T09:22:45-08:00","id":1268564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268538#post1268538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Double post, but I figured this needed its own post;<br /> <br /> The biggest hurdle WtA suffers from, compared to Vampire, is that learning the setting takes way longer. This is because WtA isn't exactly what it says on the tin. As I have stated before, garou are more a fantasy race than traditional werewolves. I have done my best to study the myths for non-WtA projects, and garou really aren't what one expects when you pick up the game called werewolf. In contrast, though VtM gets silly as all hell, in general you are still playing the expected type of vampire. You can also play vampire without getting too deep into the lore, which in WtA is pretty...well, impossible.<br /> <br /> Of course, the fix shouldn't be to make WtA darker or more brutal. It already is those things. The problem is that WtA setting is fine as it is, but it isn't going to attract many werewolf-fans with the garou being what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think I have ever met a werewolf fan who wasn't down with the majority of changes from the &quot;wolf man&quot; interpretation. Control of your powers, neat forms. The spell list of gifts might be an issue but I've never really found people who were &quot;ITCHING&quot; to play someone spend a couple nights a month special then nothing else. Werewolves as pack creatures, as even sacred warriors of nature are a rather common thing in werewolf fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T11:13:07-08:00","id":1268585,"title":"","content":"I believe that at the time WW made it clear that the only reason they were making the video game anouncement was because they legally had to under EU rules.<br /> At the time they said that there was no outline for a story, or even what sort of play style it would be--they literally had only signed paperwork to begin working with Cyanide Interactive, and Focus Home Entertainment.<br /> They then said that there wouldn't be any updates until the game was nearly ready for release.<br /> <br /> To that, everything is still following the public schedule.<br /> Yes, the game could be behind schedule, or they could be waiting to release the game around the same time as 5th Edition Werewolf (Summer 2019 perhaps?) as a tie-in product.<br /> <br /> Originally, W5 was going to be released Fall 2018 (just 6 months after V5) as well, but that was pushed back too, now without an official release date. But I don't consider W5 as Vaporware-ish. But it may be strange to release the video game before the TTRPG even has a street date itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T12:57:39-08:00","id":1268617,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the label vaporware isn't a line that signals the project is doomed. Most things that get labeled vaporware do end up never happening, but there are plenty (and even some extreme*) of cases where vaporware turns into substance. It's just that at this moment, does the project seem to be really happening, or just some &quot;smoke and mirrors&quot; to keep up the appearances of development while it's on hold for whatever reasons? Right now, there's a pretty solid case that the WtA video game is on pause/extremely low priority work, even though there's no public acknowledgement of it; thus it being vaporware. But I would put my bets in that changing after dust settles at Paradox and that we'll see it even if much later than originally hyped.<br /> <br /> * See: Duke Nukem Forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T14:15:42-08:00","id":1268634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268564#post1268564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think I have ever met a werewolf fan who wasn't down with the majority of changes from the &quot;wolf man&quot; interpretation. Control of your powers, neat forms. The spell list of gifts might be an issue but I've never really found people who were &quot;ITCHING&quot; to play someone spend a couple nights a month special then nothing else. Werewolves as pack creatures, as even sacred warriors of nature are a rather common thing in werewolf fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have run into people who don't like the whole Warriors of Gaia aspect, prerferring werewolves to be more neutral. Some don't like that werewolves cannot infect people*. Others want the wolf and the human sides to be two different entities fighting for control of the body, Others don't like that things like cannibalism aren't ok. I've met many who very much WANT their characters to struggle with the monthly change and the danger of losing control.<br /> <br /> It isn't everyone, but my point was that if you pick up Vampire you generally know what you pick. If you pick werewolf you need to read a bit more on WHAT you are playing.<br /> <br /> *The Bite from BNS isn't actually something viable in the WtA setting. Sure, it is great moral gray debate for Gaian garou. But BSDs? If THEY get it, it is just game over instantly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T20:15:18-08:00","id":1268708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268634#post1268634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have run into people who don't like the whole Warriors of Gaia aspect, prerferring werewolves to be more neutral. Some don't like that werewolves cannot infect people*. Others want the wolf and the human sides to be two different entities fighting for control of the body, Others don't like that things like cannibalism aren't ok. I've met many who very much WANT their characters to struggle with the monthly change and the danger of losing control.<br /> <br /> It isn't everyone, but my point was that if you pick up Vampire you generally know what you pick. If you pick werewolf you need to read a bit more on WHAT you are playing.<br /> <br /> *The Bite from BNS isn't actually something viable in the WtA setting. Sure, it is great moral gray debate for Gaian garou. But BSDs? If THEY get it, it is just game over instantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really the &quot;part of the month you don't have a character&quot; doesn't do much for rp. I am sure you have met people who think its a great idea.. I'm really doubting they actually would play it. Cannibalism is.. Ok? I mean as much as Diablere is in Vampire.<br /> <br /> And no I think the complex Game of thrones style politics of Vampire is as much a crazy buy in as anything in werewolf That Is a pretty BIG jump and while its eaten its way into the fabric of Vampire stories so people think its standard.. So has Warrior of Nature werewolf. I mean I don't think it would be crazy hard to explain Werewolf to someone who's seen twlight except &quot;there's white werewolves and they have more forms&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage is the one that I'd say hasn't really had as much impact I Mean &quot;Ok you're playing a game where you have magic but you can't use it. also Science is magic&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T21:24:53-08:00","id":1268721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268708#post1268708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really the &quot;part of the month you don't have a character&quot; doesn't do much for rp. I am sure you have met people who think its a great idea.. I'm really doubting they actually would play it. Cannibalism is.. Ok? I mean as much as Diablere is in Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can, if the core of the experience is about dealing with the fact you had your humanity taken away from you. I have seen people play it,too. Or put it into a short story on what happens and who gets hurt. It really isn't about playing the night of ANGER, but rather everything surrounding it, how the character deals with everything being changed. Are they part of a werewolf pack,etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T04:50:52-08:00","id":1268798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268721#post1268721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can, if the core of the experience is about dealing with the fact you had your humanity taken away from you. I have seen people play it,too. Or put it into a short story on what happens and who gets hurt. It really isn't about playing the night of ANGER, but rather everything surrounding it, how the character deals with everything being changed. Are they part of a werewolf pack,etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Being in a short story, is not the same as being as an rpg. I will say again I doubt there's this vast untapped market of people of people who want to play someone who's the supernatural equivalent of a blackout drunk.. You also probably don't need a specialized system for it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T05:02:43-08:00","id":1268800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268798#post1268798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Being in a short story, is not the same as being as an rpg. I will say again I doubt there's this vast untapped market of people of people who want to play someone who's the supernatural equivalent of a blackout drunk.. You also probably don't need a specialized system for it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've had people tell me &quot;Who the heck wants to play a human hating Gaia worshipper, why don't they just kill all humans?&quot; It isn't really about that full moon night that the RP is focused on, the werewolves can shift outside it. But it isn't like the garou instant one, their wolf self could take over. Then you play that, a feral creature that is as smart as a human but not one. There is also the moral freedom. Like I said, cannibalism for those who embrace being a monster, or mysticism.<br /> <br /> That is just one version, of course. But my point is that the garou don't as easily match what some people might expect out of werewolves. If you have found ones who are fine with the transition? Great, but that is not everyone and the Gaia Worship/humans suck aspect can be a turn off, if you want to play a tragic monster. It isn't simply a supernatural blackout drunk, it can easily be a very deep thing to explore what it is to lose ones humanity and be subjected to unnatural urges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T05:29:37-08:00","id":1268807,"title":"","content":"In the end though, for me, a new edition of WtA should be WtA, not a different werewolf game. A lot of people that want the stuff you're talking about? They should probably check out Forsaken 2e because it incorporates a lot of that as a way to separate itself from Apocalypse: You can play Harmony imbalanced characters (flesh imbalanced characters are your present standard post The Howling and American Werewolf in London werewolf film protagonists) and Harmony is in balance so you're playing out being pulled in two directions, cannibalism is totally a thing you'll probably end up doing, werewolves are quasi-infectious (though not by bites), werewolves are defined by the hunt not by being holy warriors for spirit-gods, packs are far more flexible, etc.<br /> <br /> I just really don't want to see W5 get complained about with &quot;Forsakenization,&quot; like V5 has gotten with &quot;Requiemization,&quot; where they take stuff that made the CofD games finally stand firmly apart from their equivalent WoD games, and draw them into the WoD's latest mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T05:46:18-08:00","id":1268812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268807#post1268807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end though, for me, a new edition of WtA should be WtA, not a different werewolf game. A lot of people that want the stuff you're talking about? They should probably check out Forsaken 2e because it incorporates a lot of that as a way to separate itself from Apocalypse: You can play Harmony imbalanced characters (flesh imbalanced characters are your present standard post The Howling and American Werewolf in London werewolf film protagonists) and Harmony is in balance so you're playing out being pulled in two directions, cannibalism is totally a thing you'll probably end up doing, werewolves are quasi-infectious (though not by bites), werewolves are defined by the hunt not by being holy warriors for spirit-gods, packs are far more flexible, etc.<br /> <br /> I just really don't want to see W5 get complained about with &quot;Forsakenization,&quot; like V5 has gotten with &quot;Requiemization,&quot; where they take stuff that made the CofD games finally stand firmly apart from their equivalent WoD games, and draw them into the WoD's latest mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I didn't mean that WtA should be like that. Just that the expectation for werewolves vs what WtA is, is different from vampire or mage.<br /> <br /> The problem is how to easily explain these facts without drowning the ST/players in lore. I mean, things like the Litany and the Philodox auspice alone require a lot of lore reading. An experienced ST can handle that, but a newbie one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T07:31:56-08:00","id":1268849,"title":"","content":"What if the Auspices were handled in a similar fashion to the V5 predator type? Indicating the role played in the War for Gaia, but without a lot of lore reading attached?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T08:38:27-08:00","id":1268868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268849#post1268849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Auspices were handled in a similar fashion to the V5 predator type? Indicating the role played in the War for Gaia, but without a lot of lore reading attached?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much missing the point. The auspices are ways of life, that are judged and contextualized by the life of the pack. A better way to map it out would be to give a loresheet with every auspice that gives benefits, approaches, methodologies and a nice little law cribsheet for the Philodox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T09:41:49-08:00","id":1268883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268800#post1268800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've had people tell me &quot;Who the heck wants to play a human hating Gaia worshipper, why don't they just kill all humans?&quot; It isn't really about that full moon night that the RP is focused on, the werewolves can shift outside it. But it isn't like the garou instant one, their wolf self could take over. Then you play that, a feral creature that is as smart as a human but not one. There is also the moral freedom. Like I said, cannibalism for those who embrace being a monster, or mysticism.<br /> <br /> That is just one version, of course. But my point is that the garou don't as easily match what some people might expect out of werewolves. If you have found ones who are fine with the transition? Great, but that is not everyone and the Gaia Worship/humans suck aspect can be a turn off, if you want to play a tragic monster. It isn't simply a supernatural blackout drunk, it can easily be a very deep thing to explore what it is to lose ones humanity and be subjected to unnatural urges.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if I want to play a Badass super vampire who kicks ass and takes names people have fairly consistantly called that out as &quot;bad wrong fun&quot; and definately hard to play with some of the inbuilt settings of V:TM. I Really don't see the &quot;Werewolf is super hard to sell but Vampire is easy&quot;. The Slow degeneration of you isn't an intrinsic built in of the vampire genre. There's both the &quot;you're jut a monster&quot; and &quot;you're just a person&quot; type the whole humanity thing and wassail is.. VERY unique. That's before the fact that you are a part of the Vampire Mafia/Illuminati. The ONLY reason Masquerade matches much of what we think about as Vampires is because alot of vampire fiction since then has taken from it..<br /> <br /> As for Cannibalism.. its right there. You even get some benefits for it.. YOU JUST GET IN TROUBLE FOR IT.. which really seems to be the players can't grasp cause and effect. They aren't asking for moral freedom, they are asking for Freedom from Consquences. The werewolf goes around eating people.. and then it gets killed. That's pretty much how it works. <br /> <br /> I also don't think you average would be gamer is wanting to play some sort of two character complex thing.<br /> <br /> As werewolf they want to play a guy who turns into a wolf. Is good at fighting. Has anger issues. There definately are people who want No consequences for their actions.. but that's not a &quot;Werewolf&quot; problem you get that just as readily in vampire more so because it has more consequences for your action.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T10:19:13-08:00","id":1268898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268883#post1268883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if I want to play a Badass super vampire who kicks ass and takes names people have fairly consistantly called that out as &quot;bad wrong fun&quot; and definately hard to play with some of the inbuilt settings of V:TM. I Really don't see the &quot;Werewolf is super hard to sell but Vampire is easy&quot;. The Slow degeneration of you isn't an intrinsic built in of the vampire genre. There's both the &quot;you're jut a monster&quot; and &quot;you're just a person&quot; type the whole humanity thing and wassail is.. VERY unique. That's before the fact that you are a part of the Vampire Mafia/Illuminati. The ONLY reason Masquerade matches much of what we think about as Vampires is because alot of vampire fiction since then has taken from it..<br /> <br /> As for Cannibalism.. its right there. You even get some benefits for it.. YOU JUST GET IN TROUBLE FOR IT.. which really seems to be the players can't grasp cause and effect. They aren't asking for moral freedom, they are asking for Freedom from Consquences. The werewolf goes around eating people.. and then it gets killed. That's pretty much how it works.<br /> <br /> I also don't think you average would be gamer is wanting to play some sort of two character complex thing.<br /> <br /> As werewolf they want to play a guy who turns into a wolf. Is good at fighting. Has anger issues. There definately are people who want No consequences for their actions.. but that's not a &quot;Werewolf&quot; problem you get that just as readily in vampire more so because it has more consequences for your action.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't that they don't want consequences, but rather that they don't want the same kind of society the garou have. Again, I'm not saying WtA should be like that, at all. I am saying that the people who do the Werewolf VS magazine, Werewolf News, etc. have a very different take on werewolves that would not fit WtA. That is not that WtA is bad, it is just more different from the assumed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:39:19-08:00","id":1268961,"title":"","content":"On the whole Predator Types thing:<br /> <br /> If W5 is going to include something like that, it should build off the Book of Auspices breakdown of different sub-roles that are common within each Auspice.<br /> <br /> Though I'm hesitant to think WtA needs that, because there's already way more character style choices in WtA. In VtM you have Clan, and Sect if your ST doesn't dictate Sect to you... so Predator Types help flush out vampires a bit by giving some character creation boosts to something that every vampire does need to figure out how they do by default (feeding). It's something to help not every Camarilla Toreador play on the same basic stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a default new WtA PC has Breed, Auspice, Tribe, and pack Totem to all influence how they do being a Garou. There's already a lot of variations due to having more significant basic character choices to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T15:57:32-08:00","id":1269009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268898#post1268898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It isn't that they don't want consequences, but rather that they don't want the same kind of society the garou have. Again, I'm not saying WtA should be like that, at all. I am saying that the people who do the Werewolf VS magazine, Werewolf News, etc. have a very different take on werewolves that would not fit WtA. That is not that WtA is bad, it is just more different from the assumed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I don't agree with that its more different than the basic assumptions of Vampire. Garou society is weird... so is Vampire society. I mean a Cam game basically is &quot;Hey do you want to play John WIck.. but with vampires?&quot; That's a pretty big Jump... and that's before the &quot;I want to be able to be a murder machine like Alucard in Helsing...&quot; Even Anarchs require a fairly deep dive lore and let not even get into Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I even more vehemently disagree with the idea that Werewolf less what werewolf fans expect than mage fans. Mage is the game where Harry Potter can only be kind of lucky in the Muggle world, only has real magic at hogworts... and teams up with Neo to fight Agent Smith or Rick Sanchez to fight the Terminator. Or where Sabrina teams up with Master Roshi from Dragon ball to fight the Kingpin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T15:10:17-08:00","id":1269368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1268634#post1268634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have run into people who don't like the whole Warriors of Gaia aspect, prerferring werewolves to be more neutral. Some don't like that werewolves cannot infect people*. Others want the wolf and the human sides to be two different entities fighting for control of the body, Others don't like that things like cannibalism aren't ok. I've met many who very much WANT their characters to struggle with the monthly change and the danger of losing control.<br /> <br /> It isn't everyone, but my point was that if you pick up Vampire you generally know what you pick. If you pick werewolf you need to read a bit more on WHAT you are playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, I love Garou and their portrayal was a quite profound thing for me in my youth, but I always missed the &quot;traditional&quot; werewolves from WoD. Though, honestly, I can understand it, they would share too much thematic space with Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T06:03:32-08:00","id":1269531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1269368#post1269368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truth be told, I love Garou and their portrayal was a quite profound thing for me in my youth, but I always missed the &quot;traditional&quot; werewolves from WoD. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the characteristics and traits of ' traditional ' werewolves ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T09:11:46-08:00","id":1269585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1269531#post1269531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the characteristics and traits of ' traditional ' werewolves ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, they're sharing many similarities. However, the main difference in my eyes is that garou are NOT humans and never were (no pun intended). They are a magical race of their own. Traditional werewolves were human once and don't have the strong connection to a god-like being, an inner faith, all the half-flesh-half-spirit and magical stuff and what comes with it.<br /> <br /> Even born shapeshifters (if the setting has any), those are tend to have the greater control over the animalistic side theme, but still lack all the magical and /spiritualreligious aspect Garou has and are not really a completely different race of their own.<br /> <br /> So, essentially, in my mind, &quot;traditional&quot; werewolves are the garou, minus the Gaia stuff (and a bit more emphasis on the animalistic-predatory stuff), the ingrained mission, that level of inherent magic and they're starting as humans, or as just a children of two shapeshifters, but still fully flesh, and, to some extent, &quot;human&quot; people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T09:57:14-08:00","id":1269597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1269585#post1269585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't get me wrong, they're sharing many similarities. However, the main difference in my eyes is that garou are NOT humans and never were (no pun intended). They are a magical race of their own. Traditional werewolves were human once and don't have the strong connection to a god-like being, an inner faith, all the half-flesh-half-spirit and magical stuff and what comes with it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I'm trying to say, garou are their own thing more than what is expected of werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T11:28:40-08:00","id":1269630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1269597#post1269597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is what I'm trying to say, garou are their own thing more than what is expected of werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I like them for that. WoD has unique takes on many creatures and they're great, but sometimes, I miss some &quot;traditional&quot; shapeshifters, like the ones in most urban fantasy books, or even the real, old tales and I also miss a similar kind of fae (though I was told several times that DA Fae is like that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T15:29:10-08:00","id":1269678,"title":"","content":"Granted, I believe the changes of the Garou compared to &quot;conventional&quot; werewolves in fiction was originally more of a mechanical based decision, and the fiction for it came afterwards.<br /> <br /> In a game, no player likes having their agency taking away. In this case, the idea that they, as werewolves, can't control their transformations and that it's depended on a monthly event. Or that they ALWAYS lose control of their character and basically hand it over to the GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T12:00:26-08:00","id":1270160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1269630#post1269630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I like them for that. WoD has unique takes on many creatures and they're great, but sometimes, I miss some &quot;traditional&quot; shapeshifters, like the ones in most urban fantasy books, or even the real, old tales and I also miss a similar kind of fae (though I was told several times that DA Fae is like that).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I miss the Traditonal vampires who were buried wrongly, or rose from the dead because they had a lineage of such rather than some concept of embrace... or ones that didn't have a 500 pages of wierd powers including &quot;TuRNS INTO A SNAKE&quot; and &quot;D&amp;D style fireballs&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T15:53:19-08:00","id":1270208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1270160#post1270160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I miss the Traditonal vampires who were buried wrongly, or rose from the dead because they had a lineage of such rather than some concept of embrace... or ones that didn't have a 500 pages of wierd powers including &quot;TuRNS INTO A SNAKE&quot; and &quot;D&amp;D style fireballs&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You leave my Dusk Till Dawn Culebras alone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T19:57:37-08:00","id":1270257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1270208#post1270208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You leave my Dusk Till Dawn Culebras alone!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey hey hey we can't include things that aren't a very specific view of Vampires as traditional unless they are my traditional because that's how werewolves work right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T20:04:03-08:00","id":1270258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1270257#post1270257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hey hey hey we can't include things that aren't a very specific view of Vampires as traditional unless they are my traditional because that's how werewolves work right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You...defeated me...I am...I am shamed!...I felt bad enough to be a fan of teen girl vampire hunters and daywalkers....I see I am wrong about all of them (can I post Gunship &quot;Dark All Day&quot; here? is that wrong?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T17:32:40-08:00","id":1270463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1270258#post1270258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You...defeated me...I am...I am shamed!...I felt bad enough to be a fan of teen girl vampire hunters and daywalkers....I see I am wrong about all of them (can I post Gunship &quot;Dark All Day&quot; here? is that wrong?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In a world where the most popular depiction of vampires has them coming out during the and being pedophiles with special powers and in the same damned book werewolves are magical spirit indians clearly werewolf is too complicated and vampire is &quot;just right&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T17:55:53-08:00","id":1270468,"title":"","content":"For me, I like all the different ways these creatures have been told and retold over the years. I didn't mean to come off as rude as my posts may have come across (I've reread them). There has been a large amount of variety in how werewolves, vampires and others have been depicted over the years. I'm not big on the idea that &quot;these things aren't like the creatures of the middle age stories&quot;. I know for some people it can be fun, but it always seems like those people seem to say it in ways that sound like other variations on these creatures are somehow less valid and not the right &quot;fun&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T18:08:53-08:00","id":1270475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1270258#post1270258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You...defeated me...I am...I am shamed!...I felt bad enough to be a fan of teen girl vampire hunters and daywalkers....I see I am wrong about all of them (can I post Gunship &quot;Dark All Day&quot; here? is that wrong?)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing wrong with being a fan of Buffy, the only teenage girl vampire slayer series.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1270463#post1270463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In a world where the most popular depiction of vampires has them coming out during the and being pedophiles with special powers and in the same damned book werewolves are magical spirit indians clearly werewolf is too complicated and vampire is &quot;just right&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can all agree that Twilight was single worst thing to ever happen to vampires and werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T05:17:35-08:00","id":1270802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1270475#post1270475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we can all agree that Twilight was single worst thing to ever happen to vampires and werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>X1,000. I absolutely refuse to read or watch anything having to do with Twilight. It deserves every bit of mockery and disdain ever foisted upon it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.darthsanddroids.net/episodes/0572.html\" target=\"_blank\">And vampires <i>do not sparkle in the daylight</i>!</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T19:41:49-08:00","id":1271021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1270802#post1270802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> X1,000. I absolutely refuse to read or watch anything having to do with Twilight. It deserves every bit of mockery and disdain ever foisted upon it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.darthsanddroids.net/episodes/0572.html\" target=\"_blank\">And vampires <i>do not sparkle in the daylight</i>!</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yet that's pretty much the potential audience for this game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T14:53:31-08:00","id":1271266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1265975#post1265975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every single time the Garou let their Rage and pride get the better of them, they (and Gaia) paid a <i>very</i> heavy price for it. The Garou didn't get off scot-free once. ... the Garou become their own worst enemies if they keep letting their Rage get the better of them.<br /> ...<br /> How will you deal with the fuckups of your ancestors? Will you try to make up for them? And if you try, do you even have a chance of succeeding? And if not, what then?</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, my personal opinion is that it's their <i>pride</i>, not their <i>rage</i>, that makes the Garou their own worst enemies. They make things worse not so much by raging, but by considering themselves better than everyone else and bullying whoever doesn't fall in line. They didn't start the Impergium as an outlet for rage, but as a way to control the human population (ironically the Garou were behaving more like the weaver than the wyld in that case). The Garou didn't start the War of Rage because they believed it was right to commit genocide, but because they believed it was their divine right to rule all the Fera, and the other changing breeds' resistance to their dominion was foolish ignorance. They can get carried away in their rage, but their greatest sins have always started as reactions to wounded pride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T07:06:54-08:00","id":1271432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1265029-werewolf-5th-edition?p=1271266#post1271266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For what it's worth, my personal opinion is that it's their <i>pride</i>, not their <i>rage</i>, that makes the Garou their own worst enemies. They make things worse not so much by raging, but by considering themselves better than everyone else and bullying whoever doesn't fall in line....They can get carried away in their rage, but their greatest sins have always started as reactions to wounded pride.</div> </div> </div> </div>All quite true. Both their Rage and their pride have gotten the Garou into more trouble than was necessary. It's probably academic, but it might be more accurate to say that it's hubris, rather than pride, that caused the Garou's downfall. But I'm defining &quot;hubris as &quot;arrogant pride&quot; so the difference is only one of semantic degree. But wounded pride feeding into the Garou's rage (and Rage) is definitely a big theme in W:tA.<br /> <br /> If wounded pride or a loss of face comes about as a fear of losing power, then what Yoda said in Star Wars applies equally in W:tA as well: &quot;Fear leads to anger. Anger leads to hate. Hate leads to suffering.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T22:36:24-08:00","id":1272783,"title":"","content":"Hrrm, I think that hybris is more a defining trait of the Mage game line.<br /> Werewolves start the war of rage because they rashly decide the Gurhali slighted them on purpose, exterminate whole Fera breeds because they &quot;look different&quot;, cull humans because they are afraid of the Weaver rise... the whole Garou background is about following paranoias because no one took ten minutes to speak to the other side trying to understand them and settle things up. I'd say that more than anything they're impulsive, pride and honour are just secondary traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}